    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-019: Back and Forward Navigation** -- the specification for wiring up the Back (`←`) and Forward (`→`) toolbar buttons, which are currently stubs that print `غير مُفعَّل بعد` to the status bar.\n\nDocumentation only. Implementation (3 commits) lands in a follow-up PR after this ADR is reviewed and merged.\n\n## What the ADR specifies\n\n**`NavigationHistory` helper class** (`src/browser/navigation_history.hpp`) -- a vector of URLs plus a cursor. `push()` truncates forward history and appends; `back()` / `forward()` move the cursor and return the newly-current URL. Pure data structure, no GTK, unit-testable.\n\n**`NavKind` discriminator** in `HoneyBeeWindow::navigate_to(url, NavKind)`:\n\n| `NavKind` | History mutation | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|\n| `New` | push on success | URL bar Enter, click link |\n| `Back` | cursor left | Back button |\n| `Forward` | cursor right | Forward button |\n| `Reload` | none | Reload button |\n\nReload bypasses history so pressing it N times doesn't create N entries (which would make Back useless).\n\n## Design decisions worth flagging\n\n- **Push-on-success, not optimistic**: a failed fetch doesn't enter history.\n- **Rollback on failure for Back/Forward**: if going back to page X fails, cursor reverts.\n- **No page cache**: back re-fetches. Caching is deferred to a future ADR.\n- **`:visited` needs no change**: `record_visit` fires on every successful load, and `visited_urls` is a set, so re-insertion is idempotent.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Page caching (back re-fetches)\n- Scroll position restoration\n- History persistence across sessions\n- History length cap\n- History UI (dropdown, right-click)\n- Keyboard shortcuts (Alt+Left / Alt+Right)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] Data model is right (`NavigationHistory` API sensible?)\n- [ ] `NavKind` captures all cases (is `Reload` really distinct from `New`?)\n- [ ] Failure rollback policy acceptable\n- [ ] Deferred items in the right place\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched, so no test changes. Will run `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` after merge to confirm `main` still clean (237 cases, 905 assertions, unchanged).\n",
